Id: nfs007w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_exports
Fix: Name the clients that may mount it.
References: exports(5)
Controls: CIS 3.3, 4.8; NIST AC-3, CM-7; ISO 8.3, 8.21; CE Secure configuration

Exporting a directory to everyone means that anyone can
look at your files.  The information gained can possibly
be used to gain further access to the machine.

On Linux, everyone is '*', an option list with no host before it
('/srv (rw)', and the '(rw)' of '/srv host (rw)', where a blank
parts it from the host), a path with no client after it, and
0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0. The files are read as exportfs reads them:
/etc/exports, then /etc/exports.d/*.exports.

See `nfs013i'
